@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* SiteNav's Overview, written by hand after AppShell's and AppSidebar's: links that fold into a
   menu, what goes under them, and SiteNav beside a sidebar, each a page of its own in a frame with a
   phone width. Parts, Accessibility and See also come from the metadata and the doc comments; See
   also adds the content site demo. *@

<TextBlock>A site nav is a row of links in an <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-shell">AppShell</Anchor>'s header. It suits a site with no sidebar. Its links are <Code>NavItem</Code>s, marked current on the server as in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/nav-menu">NavMenu</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Links that fold into a menu</Heading>
<TextBlock>On narrow screens, the links fold into a menu button that opens them in a panel under the header. The same button closes the panel, so the header with the site's name stays in view. The links fold below 768px by default; to change that width, set <Code>Breakpoint</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="site-nav-usage" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>The panel is a native popover, so it opens and closes with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>, and Escape or a tap outside closes it. With IzzyBlazor's script, opening the panel moves focus to the first link, and following a link closes it.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Under the links</Heading>
<TextBlock>The panel can have content under the links, such as a call-to-action button. Add a <Code>SiteNavFooter</Code>. It shows only on phones, in the panel.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Footer</Code>
<TextBlock>On wide screens the footer isn't shown, so put anything the user needs there somewhere else on the page as well.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">With a sidebar</Heading>
<TextBlock>A site nav can sit in the header of a shell with an <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-sidebar">AppSidebar</Anchor>, for links to the rest of the site beside the app's own. On phones, its menu button stays hidden, and the links show at the top of the sidebar's drawer or panel instead, so there's one menu.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@WithSidebar</Code>
<TextBlock>The <Anchor Href="demos/app-sidebar/menu-panel">guide demo</Anchor> has site links over a sidebar of chapters.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Where the menu button goes</Heading>
<TextBlock>On phones, the menu button sits at the end of the header, where users look for it, whatever comes after the links. To put it before the brand, such as on pages whose header starts with a <Code>SidebarToggle</Code>, set <Code>MenuButtonPosition</Code> to <Code>Start</Code>. To leave it where the links are, set <Code>InPlace</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The landmark and the menu button have names for screen readers. The landmark's default differs from a sidebar's "Main". To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Label</Code></td><td>The navigation landmark's name</td><td>"Site"</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>MenuLabel</Code></td><td>The menu button's name</td><td>"Menu"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string WithSidebar = """
        <AppShell>
            <AppHeader>
                <SidebarToggle />
                <AppBrand Href="/" Icon="Lucide.Zap" Label="Acme" />
                <Box Grow />
                <SiteNav>
                    <NavItem Href="/guide">Guide</NavItem>
                    <NavItem Href="/blog">Blog</NavItem>
                </SiteNav>
            </AppHeader>
            <AppSidebar>
                <NavMenu>...</NavMenu>
            </AppSidebar>
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
        </AppShell>
        """;

    private const string Footer = """
        <SiteNav>
            <NavItem Href="/projects">Projects</NavItem>
            <NavItem Href="/articles">Articles</NavItem>
            <SiteNavFooter>
                <Button Href="/signup" FullWidth>Sign up</Button>
            </SiteNavFooter>
        </SiteNav>
        """;
}
